# GOLDEN RA RB POSSIBLY
# GOLDEN-SUBSET RA RB NO
# GROUND-TRUTH: the constant-fold twin of presence_02. `abs(E) >= -5` is true
#   of every real E, so the encoder folded the whole comparison to `true`
#   BEFORE linearizing - and a region whose encoding is `true` is a superset of
#   everything. It is FALSE for the same reason: `abs(dxy(eles[0])) >= -5` is a
#   comparison, and a comparison over an absent property is a decidable FALSE,
#   so an electron with no `dxy` is In RA and not in RB.
#
#   Under the presence model the fold produces the PRESENCE LITERAL rather than
#   `true`: `|x| > k` for negative k IS exactly the definedness of x. The
#   quantities come from the subtree, since nothing was linearized.

object eles
  take Ele
  select pt > 20

region RA
  select size(eles) >= 1

region RB
  select abs(dxy(eles[0])) >= -5
